  "id": "COMPOUND:307 - PROTEIN:2120",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between gefitinib and (S)-2-haloacid dehalogenase, mediated through flavopiridol and staurosporine. Gefitinib is reported to target Atypical kinase COQ8B, mitochondrial, which in turn is a target of flavopiridol, and flavopiridol also targets (S)-2-haloacid dehalogenase. Similarly, gefitinib is reported to target IL13 protein, which is a target of flavopiridol, and flavopiridol also targets (S)-2-haloacid dehalogenase. Additionally, gefitinib is reported to target PT-45, which is a target of staurosporine, and staurosporine also targets (S)-2-haloacid dehalogenase. These findings suggest that (S)-2-haloacid dehalogenase may be a downstream target of multiple drugs, including gefitinib, through a common pathway involving flavopiridol. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which gefitinib could influence (S)-2-haloacid dehalogenase, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
